   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to authorizing the performance\nof certain dental hygiene services at voluntary foster care agency health\nfacilities",
    "basePrintNo": "S8784",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8784-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§6606 & 6608, Ed L (as proposed in S.3157 & A.2341)",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8784\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to authorizing the\nperformance of certain dental hygiene services at voluntary foster care\nagency health facilities\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to the provisions of\nL.2025, C.682.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by allowing voluntary\nfoster care agency health facilities licensed under Article 29i of\npublic health law to be one of the settings where dental hygienists can\nperform services under the collaborative practice agreement.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 682 of the Laws of 2025.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENT:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2025 amending the education law relating to\nregistered dental hygienists working without supervision but within a\ncollaborative practice agreement with a licensed dentist, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers 5.3157 and A.2341, takes effect.\n",
